4 0 obj
<<
/Creator ( )
/Producer ( )
/Author ()
/Keywords (*ARMY OPERATIONS;CEREALS;DETECTORS;SMALL ARMS AMMUNITION;HELICOPTERS;TACTICAL AIR SUPPORT;SMALL ARMS;LOGISTICS;CASUALTIES;WOUNDS AND INJURIES;MILITARY TRAINING;VIETNAM;ARTILLERY FIRE;AIRMOBILE OPERATIONS;COUNTERINSURGENCY;ENEMY PERSONNEL;CAMBODIA;DEPLOYMENT;DETECTION)
/Subject (During this reporting period the 1st Cav Div AM conducted a coordinated attack against the COSVN Base area in the Fishhook region of Cambodia. Subsequent seize and interdict operations were conducted throughout the Cambodian AO followed by a phased withdrawal and a redeployment of forces. Operations were continued throughout the AO to interdict enemy infiltration routes through Phuoc Long, Binh Long, Binh Dong, Bien Hoa and Long Khanh Provinces in order to deny enemy access to the population centers and to neutralize enemy forces operating in the area. Division elements continued to support the GVN Pacification Program and conducted Dong Tien operations with RVNAF forces operating within the Division AO.)
/Title (Lessons Learned, Headquarters, 1st Cavalry Division \(Airmobile\))
/Filename (/pdf/TR/AD0514580.pdf)
>>
